  "verified_on": "2026-11-19",
  "abstract_html": "<p>For a two-term complex <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> of generalized Kronecker quiver representations, we prove exponential cancellation of its acyclic part under the polar-phase interpretation of the minimizing flow of Haiden, Katzarkov, Kontsevich and Pandit. Suppose the differential <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>:</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></math> is surjective, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>&#x02260;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>, and the cohomology <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>ker</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> is nonzero at both vertices. For all vertex charges in the upper half-plane and every initial Hermitian metric, the endomorphism defining the flow approaches that of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow></math> exponentially in trace norm, with the induced metric on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow></math> and extension by zero. If the source charge has larger argument than the target charge and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow></math> is polystable, the induced metric multiplied by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>arg</mi><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math> converges exponentially to a harmonic metric, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> is the central charge of the cohomology. In this chamber semistability suffices for the shifted moment map to tend to zero. The arrow-energy estimate uses the kernel of second divided differences of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></math> at the nodes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>&#x02113;</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><msub><mi>&#x02113;</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>&#x02113;</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>. Its Schur product <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>J</mi></mrow></math> with any positive semidefinite matrix satisfies <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>tr</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo></msub><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>tr</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo></msub></mrow></math> is the negative part. We also prove that, at fixed positive definite imaginary part, minus the polar phase is strictly monotone for the trace inner product.</p>",
